\title{imagefilter: Apply Colour Filters to Bitmap Images}
\description{
The imagefilter package provides functions for converting RGB
bitmap images into greyscale, red, green, blue, and black-and-magenta
versions.
}
\details{
The filter functions process one RGB pixel at a time. The
\code{apply_filter()} function applies a selected filter to every pixel
in a bitmap image.
}
\section{Filter functions}{

\code{grey_filter()} converts a pixel to greyscale.

\code{red_filter()} converts a pixel to a red version.

\code{green_filter()} converts a pixel to a green version.

\code{blue_filter()} converts a pixel to a blue version.

\code{cutoff_filter()} applies a black-and-magenta cut-off.
}

\section{Whole-image functions}{

\code{apply_filter()} applies a selected pixel filter to every pixel
of a bitmap image and returns the filtered bitmap.

\code{apply_image_filter()} takes a magick image, converts its first
frame to a bitmap, calls \code{apply_filter()}, and converts the
filtered bitmap back to a magick image.
}

\section{Usage}{

Read an image with \code{magick::image_read()}, then pass it to
\code{apply_image_filter()} together with a pixel filter, for example:

\code{plot(apply_image_filter(my_object, grey_filter))}
}

